WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.090
Can you imagine...

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:16.300
...a life in which you could
never touch the one you love?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.560
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.980
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.850
His own mother has
distanced herself from him.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.190
His friends have called him a monster.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:31.360
Even strangers have spoken of him as the
Death incarnate that dwells in the forest.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.030
And yet,

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.200
he doesn't feel the least bit lonely.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.910
I'd like to give a gift to Rob.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.580
Do you have any good ideas?

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.580
Hmm...

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.960
How about reading glasses?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.540
Nuh-uh, no way, no way.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.130
Glasses are out of the question.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.630
I want us to be able to look

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.260
directly into each other's eyes,
not through a pair of lenses.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.970
Well then, what about a handkerchief?

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.930
Great idea! Thanks, Alice!

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:01.810
She's a romantic.
Just like you, Your Grace.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.990
Today's Christmas Eve, huh...

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:43.280
"Episode 9: The Duke, Alice,
and the Christmas Eve Vow"
So, that's why I got word from Viola
ahead of time that she'll be here today.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.330
And why she's giving Rob a gift.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.790
Lady Viola's such a brave girl.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:52.580
But I'm a little disappointed that
we can't spend Christmas Eve

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.710
alone together, Your Grace.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.760
I'm just going to go lock all of
the doors to the mansion real quick!

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.680
Please, come back! I was only kidding!

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.760
Cuff and Zain are also planning
on dropping by later on.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.020
Looks like we'll be having
a Christmas party tonight.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.680
Oh? A party, huh?

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.690
You think it's okay for me to take part
in such a normal human activity?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.190
Well, you always have been
a human, you know.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.320
But we're talking about
a Christmas party here.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.570
And here I am wearing
the same old hat and clothes.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.660
Your outfit's just fine the way it is.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.620
Though I decided to put on
my best pair just in case.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.870
--Of underwear, that is.
--Huh?! What's with the see-through...

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.790
Yoo-hoo!

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.500
Merry Xmas, Mother.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.710
It seems you've been
going out a lot lately.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.760
Yes, well, I've had things to do.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.260
I don't know where
you've been going exactly,

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.600
but Christmas is a time
to be spent with family.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.560
Stay home today.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.930
Yes, Mother.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.140
And another thing...

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:56.480
How much longer do you intend
to wear such childish attire?

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:03.240
I'm sorry, Mother.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.370
Get everything ready for
my departure as planned.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.540
But the lady of the house
told you not to...

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.330
It's okay as long as I spend
the time with family, right?

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.670
And I don't need you guys
tagging along, either.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.010
I'll be fine as long as I have my driver.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.300
She's going to see Rob.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:32.430
It's Christmas, and she's planning on
going to that creep's place again?

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.690
Making a two-hour special trip...

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.980
Two... Two!

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.610
Oh, dear! His secondborn son
complex is acting up again!

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.280
What a strong core he's got!

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.200
You call it a party,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.160
but we don't even have a tree,

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.160
nor anything else to put us
in the Christmas spirit.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.790
You're right.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.670
It would be nice if we had
a Santa Claus, at least...

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.960
Santa, huh?

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.210
Your Grace?

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.460
Your Grace?

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.090
Your Grace?

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.640
Your Grace?

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.180
Mwah!

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.430
Mwah! Mwah! Mwah!

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.520
What do you see in there?

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.990
It may not be very Christmassy, but
I'll try to serve the best meal I can.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.950
I think we'll have a jolly old time.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.410
Yeah, I'm really glad.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.170
I got Rob a nice handkerchief
that I think will suit him well.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.920
I hope I can work up
the nerve to give it to him.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.930
Lord Walter, it is really all right for
me to let you drive the carriage?

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:56.770
This is the perfect opportunity to find
out how that accursed firstborn is doing.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.600
It appears Viola doesn't suspect a thing.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.230
Just you wait, you miserable
excuse for an older brother.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:04.150
The one who'll inherit the family title...

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.900
...is me!

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.450
I just felt a shiver go down my spine.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.370
Oh, my! That's awful!

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.830
Shall we warm each other
with our body heat?

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.040
I can't!

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:19.580
We're coming in!

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:20.960
Merry Xmas!

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.040
Welcome, Cuff and Zain!

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.260
Hey, Alice, long time no see!

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.220
I see your boobs are as big as ever.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:30.800
We brought you something.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.930
Why, it's a Christmas tree!

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.810
Thank you.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:37.520
We were just thinking about what
we were going to do for a tree.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:41.230
Let's deck the halls so fancy
that it'll knock Santa's boots off!

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:42.440
Wait, Santa?

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:43.770
Huh?

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.190
This may be the year
I'll actually get to see him!

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.860
I guess there are even
witches who believe he exists.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:54.280
Okay, why don't you help me
decorate the tree, Alice?

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.950
--Ooh-ooh! If Alice is helping, then I want to, too!
--Certainly.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.540
--Nope, Zain.
--No way, Zain.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.330
Did you guys really have
to be so emphatic about it?

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.290
Well, this place is so drab.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:08.130
Let's leave the tree to the ladies
and decorate the room instead,

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.380
Thigh Guy!

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.470
Heck yeah!

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.090
Thigh Guy?!

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.730
Hmm...

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.440
I guesstimate she's a J.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.610
Hey, watch it!

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:26.980
Changing the subject,

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.030
don't you think it's kind of hard for two
people to decorate the whole room?

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.240
--It'd be better if the four of us did it.
--Comin' through...

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.240
Are you telling me you'd make
the ladies do that hard work?

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:37.910
Huh? Yeah, I see your point.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.080
You're actually saying
something decent for once...

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.870
Aw, cut me some slack!

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.920
Besides whenever you ask
Cuff to do anything hard,

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.750
it only makes more work for you.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.250
This is impossible!

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:51.340
You see, she can't do much of anything.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.260
The only thing she's got
going for her is that she's cute.

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:55.430
Oh, so you acknowledge that.

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:56.600
What the heck is this?

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:01.640
And she can't tell a lie,
and she's got a big heart.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.350
--And she's kind of sexy...
--Enough already!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:04.560
Why don't you tell her how you feel?

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:05.980
I couldn't do that.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:08.820
For better or worse,

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:12.610
she's been that way since she was a kid.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:15.530
Thanks for being Cuff's friend and all...

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:18.540
Huh? Well, I'm the one who
should be thanking you guys...

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.330
But enough about that.
Let's play some pranks...

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:22.580
...on Alice!

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:23.830
Absolutely not!

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.630
For example, and I'm just
throwing this out there,

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:31.170
what if this shiny ribbon here just
happened to get wrapped around Alice?

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:36.970
Don't you think it would
look totally sexy and cute?

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.180
Wow, I wonder how that got there!

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.850
I know, right?

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:49.980
Or, what if this were the only thing that
just happened to adorn her naked body?

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.360
I guess she heard me.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.660
You never learn, do you?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.660
It's all done.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.580
Hey, Zain! Wake up! Wake up!

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.040
Zain, come take a look!

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:13.880
I've got Alice to thank for doing most of
the work, but I also helped out a little!

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.590
Hey, nice work there.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.050
So, what do you think?

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:20.510
There isn't anything as pretty as this
in all the witches' world, is there?

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.270
Why don't you tell her how you feel?

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.400
It sure is pretty.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:38.320
A-And so are you, Cuff...

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:43.790
Huh?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:45.000
Zzz!

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.460
She's asleep standing up?!

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.960
Just a moment ago she said
she was going to take a nap

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:51.290
because Santa would be coming
in the middle of the night.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.380
What the--?!

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.760
She picked the absolute
worst time to do it!

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.720
I'll find her a more
suitable place to sleep.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.800
Up you go! There you are.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:00.970
That's some rough handling there...

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:02.260
It's all right.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:06.770
I shouldn't have done something
that was out of my depth.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.440
I'll make us some tea.

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.440
Thanks, Alice!

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.820
Oh, I wish I could live a life
as easygoing as Cuff's.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.110
Your life seems pretty easygoing to me.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:18.450
You think?

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:25.870
Even Walter's not here...

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:36.380
I'm here!

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.130
She's in an awfully big hurry.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:41.340
Does she want to see that
infernal firstborn that bad?

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.350
What's that?

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.100
Viola must have dropped it.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.850
Don't tell me it's for him!

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.480
Darn you, firstborn!

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:57.110
This is just what I expected the home
of a Death incarnate to be like.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:58.570
It's Christmas...

00:10:58.570 --> 00:10:59.990
...and the place is deserted.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:06.870
I hear the only people that live in this
mansion are him and his two servants.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.410
I know it's because of his curse,
but still, it's kind of sad.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:15.210
It just goes to show that I'm better
suited to inherit the family title.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:19.880
I must be very, very quiet...

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.470
Hold on--
What's a Santa suit doing here?!

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.020
Is it some kind of trap?

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.480
And...

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:30.520
...why does it come with a fake beard?!

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:31.810
--Oh?
--Huh?

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.860
You must be Santa!

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.690
OMG, OMG, OMG, OMG, OMG!

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:41.400
--It's the first time I've seen
you in the flesh!
--Wh-What do you mean?

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.570
What?

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.580
You aren't Santa?
Who are you, anyway?

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.410
Um, uh, well...

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:49.750
Why, I'm Santa, of course!

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.370
Wow!

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:52.920
Santa! It <i>is </i>you!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:54.790
Did you come here to deliver our presents?

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:55.960
Um, well...

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:58.920
Here's your present.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.630
This is the first time someone's
ever given me a present.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:05.600
--You really <i>are </i>Santa!
--Darn it! That was Viola's.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.180
Okay, well, Santa's a busy guy,
so I'll be seeing you.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.720
Are you going to make your
round-the-world trip now?

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:10.890
Yeah, that's right. See you!

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.350
If you're leaving, that means you've
got your flying reindeer sleigh, right?

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.980
--Show it to me.
--Yeah, well, I didn't ride it here today.

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.400
That means I couldn't use
the chimney to get in.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:19.730
Okay, I mean it this time.
This really is goodbye!

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.000
Need a lift to the chimney?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.410
Are you a witch?!

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:33.370
Well, you're practically one
of us yourself, eh, Santa?

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:42.970
That's weird. Where could I
have dropped Rob's gift?

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:45.720
This sucks.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:46.850
Hey, there!

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.390
Did you find what you were looking for?

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:50.930
I'll try again later.

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:54.730
Oh, this mask's so nice and fluffy!
It's really soothing!

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.730
Oh, yeah!

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:02.990
Ho! Ho! Ho! Merry Christmas!

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:05.530
Hey, Rob, what's with you?

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:08.030
Ho! Ho! Ho!

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:13.830
We got a Santa suit ready to surprise
Cuff with, but we seem to have lost it.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.460
So, you're trying to make do
by mimicking him?

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.250
Ho! Ho! Ho!

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.460
Huh? Where's Cuff?

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.010
She woke up and went
off looking for Santa.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.800
--Oh, dear.
--Ho! Ho! Ho!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.590
--We get the point! Is that your pet phrase now?
--Rob's so cute!

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:30.430
--Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!
--Oh, where's the gift I brought?

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.520
My Christmas is ruined!

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.390
Oh, this is so soothing!

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:36.230
Viola, that's a little...

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:53.120
Ho! Ho! Ho!

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:54.950
Merry Christmas!

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.250
Santa's here!

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.760
That's a bit of a stretch.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:05.760
Honestly, I don't believe it!

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:09.090
You followed me here, Walter?

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.600
Walter? As in, my younger brother?!

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.690
D... D-D-D...

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:21.940
Don't call me your younger brother!

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:24.320
Call me your rival!

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:27.820
Huh?

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:29.910
Your R-I-V-A-L!

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:32.990
Why did he come wearing a Santa suit?

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:35.750
And why did he come down the chimney?

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:40.170
I haven't seen you in years, and yet
I see you haven't changed a bit.

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:42.630
You look pretty chic yourself, Walter.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.090
I'm so jealous.

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:47.510
The last thing I want to hear is
you telling me you're jealous!

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:50.180
Viola, why do you like this creep?

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:53.470
First off, why don't you tell everyone
you're sorry for crashing the party?

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.060
Just look at how dirty the floor is!

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.890
Er... I'm sorry.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.310
I don't know what's gotten
into that head of yours,

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:00.560
but you're a real pain, you know that?

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.360
It's not like I came to our brother's
place because I'm fond of him or anything.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:08.320
Not fond of him, not fond of him, not fond
of him, not fond of him, not fond of him.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.160
Looks like one extra person
got his feelings hurt.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.870
This guy's a friend of
that witch I just met.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:19.910
I'm amazed that firstborn here knows these
witches and still can't break his curse.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:21.540
Just look at him.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.130
Mother's too easy on him.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.130
Even if he could break his curse,

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.840
he's not fit to be the head of the family.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:31.930
Huh?

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:32.930
Where's Santa?

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.100
He left.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.260
Who the heck are you?

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.350
Hmm?

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:39.390
Ah!

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:43.230
Hey, that's mine!
I'm so glad you found it!

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:44.770
No, you're wrong.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:46.440
This is a gift from Santa.

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:47.440
What?!

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:51.360
There don't appear to be any problems,
so let's get dinner ready.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:52.530
All right.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.070
Give that back!

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:55.490
No way!

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:57.950
I think I'll get some shut-eye.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.290
It's like a free space in here...

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.460
It seems you can't even
take command of this room.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.250
Do you really intend to
inherit the family title?

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:09.300
That's a very precious item!

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.760
Santa gave it to <i>me</i>!

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:16.430
Well, since I am the firstborn son
and all, I guess I'd like to inherit it.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:19.390
That is, if I can break this curse,
and the family welcomes me back.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:20.850
Where did you find this?

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:22.640
What are you talking about?
Santa gave me this.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:24.520
Do you really expect me to believe that?

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:25.860
You've really got it easy.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.150
Has anyone ever told you that
you were someone else's alternate?

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:31.740
Ah-choo!

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.780
How do you think they've treated
me for over a decade?

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:36.780
How should I know?

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:42.330
I'm your alternate. Just in case
your curse can't be broken.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:45.830
I've got plenty of replacements for you!

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:51.510
Just because I was born a little later,
your existence determines my whole future.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.720
I don't care one way or the other!

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.380
It's my first present!

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.430
--Oh, come on!
--I'll hear you out after I patch things up.

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:59.350
By all means...

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.020
Hey, don't you know?

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:04.520
That flower-like part...

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:07.940
...makes you grow a beard and break
out in a rash all over. It's poisonous.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.150
You'd better let go of it.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:12.030
Really? That's awful!

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:14.360
I'll take care of it. Stand back, Viola!

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.360
Hey!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.370
What do you think you're doing?!

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.740
Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:21.750
Are you all right?

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:24.040
I've got gloves on, so I'm okay!

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:28.590
It should be good to go
once you rewrap it.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.380
Here you go, Viola.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.710
You're okay with this, aren't you Cuff?

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:35.430
Yep. I'm sorry I tried to
keep it all to myself.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:38.800
I know it's not poisonous now,
so I'll let you have it, Viola.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.140
Thanks.

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.220
It was mine to begin with, though.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.890
And, um... Dearest Brother?

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.230
Thank you, too.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:49.230
Huh?!

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:51.900
That's the first time you ever
thanked me for anything, Viola...

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:53.780
Er, well...

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:56.910
So, anyway, how did you
make that fireball just now?

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:59.450
Well, I am a performer, you know.
It's top secret.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:00.450
Oh, really?

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:02.580
I'll make you a friendly wager.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:06.920
The first of us to uncover the truth about
your curse inherits the family title.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:09.670
The loser remains
an alternate for all time.

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:13.670
I'm not sure I follow you, but if that's
what you want to do, then all right.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:14.840
I accept.

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:19.050
Okay, so it's settled, then.

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.550
Farewell!

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:21.180
Huh?!

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:22.180
Oops!

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:25.890
Hey!

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:27.190
Oh, jeez, he knocked over the tree.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:29.150
You'd better fix all the
decorations before you go!

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:31.650
He tries to act cool
but can't quite pull it off.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:42.080
<i>Outside a powdery snow is falling</i>

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.540
<i>And when Santa's reindeer sleigh</i>

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:48.000
<i>Flies across the night sky</i>

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.880
<i>The lights in the windows</i>

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:54.340
<i>Turn on one by one</i>

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:59.220
<i>And look like stars scattered</i>
<i>throughout the town</i>

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.680
<i>We decorate our Christmas tree</i>

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:04.140
<i>With ornaments galore</i>

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:08.140
<i>Carefully so it's well-balanced</i>

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:11.190
<i>And as our hearts sing "Jingle Bells"</i>
<i>Yes, "Jingle Bells"</i>

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:13.650
<i>We place a twinkling star on top</i>

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.940
<i>And then the party begins</i>

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:23.320
<i>If there's such a thing as</i>
<i>a Christmas miracle</i>

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:27.700
<i>We'd like everybody to be smiling</i>

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:33.250
<i>All over the world for just this moment</i>

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:38.470
<i>With all our hearts we make a wish</i>

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.840
Aw, man!

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:43.760
I just remembered I can't
go back without Viola.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.180
I'm freezing...

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:52.020
Everyone's gone.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:55.070
I never thought I'd meet Walter tonight.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:57.480
He seems like an interesting guy.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:02.860
Now that the party's over,
there's nothing else to do for Christmas.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:05.160
Oh, but there is.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:11.040
On Christmas, it's okay to ask for
a kiss underneath the mistletoe.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.420
So, let's give each other a kiss.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:13.750
But I can't!

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:15.380
Whoops!

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:16.380
Oh, dear.

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.380
Are you able to stand?

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:23.470
On that day, too...

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:24.930
On that day, too...

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:27.760
...I was covered in snow...

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:32.020
...and about ready to die.
But then you came.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:35.400
And everything changed inside me.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:40.990
Alice, I like you, I think...

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.070
Um, uh...

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:48.950
You must think I'm weird for saying
this out of the blue and all.

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.040
Um... er...

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.250
I-I'm sorry.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.290
I... uh...

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:00.210
I'm so sorry.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:05.050
Don't be. It surprised me, that's all.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:10.140
I-I'm going to live.

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:12.270
Together, with you.

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:17.810
That's how I want to live.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.730
I've got friends.

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:22.400
I even hosted a party.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:24.780
I've got you and Viola and Rob.

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:29.160
There are so many things that
make me glad I didn't give in.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:31.200
And I have you to thank for it.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:34.290
Thank you for those delightful words.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:38.000
I'll accept them as your
Christmas gift to me.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.840
And in return...

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:43.920
...I give myself to you.

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:48.050
You scared me half to death!

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:51.060
I wonder what happened to
the pure you of those days.

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:53.930
Hey, doesn't that feel cold to you?

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:58.150
I wanted to share in the coldness
you're feeling, Your Grace.

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:02.280
Because we're going to
go on living together.

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:05.950
I stand corrected.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:08.200
You're just as pure as ever.

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:11.030
Really?

00:23:42.790 --> 00:23:46.340
"The Duke, Alice, and a Song for Two."
